    "id": "train-3797",
    "question": "Ivan had $10 and spent 1/5 of it on cupcakes. He then spent some money on a milkshake and had only $3 left. How much is the milkshake?",
    "gold": "5",
    "answer": "Ivan spent a total of $10 - $3 = $<<10-3=7>>7 on cupcakes and a milkshake.\nThe cost of the cupcake is $10 x 1/5 = $<<10*1/5=2>>2.\nSo, $7 - $2 = $<<7-2=5>>5 was spent on the milkshake.\n#### 5"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much money Ivan spent on the milkshake, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate how much money Ivan spent on cupcakes.\n2. Determine how much money Ivan had after buying the cupcakes.\n3. Find out how much money Ivan spent on the milkshake.\n\nStep 1: Calculate how much money Ivan spent on cupcakes.\nIvan started with $10 and spent \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) of it on cupcakes. So, the amount spent on cupcakes is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5} \\times 10 = 2\n\\]\nTherefore, Ivan spent $2 on cupcakes.\n\nStep 2: Determine how much money Ivan had after buying the cupcakes.\nAfter spending $2 on cupcakes, the amount of money Ivan had left is:\n\\[\n10 - 2 = 8\n\\]\nSo, Ivan had $8 left after buying the cupcakes.\n\nStep 3: Find out how much money Ivan spent on the milkshake.\nIvan had $3 left after buying the milkshake. Therefore, the amount spent on the milkshake is:\n\\[\n8 - 3 = 5\n\\]\nSo, Ivan spent $5 on the milkshake.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
